          "solution": "For small angles the $n$-th minimum is at $\\theta_n\\approx\\frac{n\\lambda}d$. The separation between the 2nd minimum on one side and the 3rd on the other is $\\theta=\\theta_2+\\theta_3=\\frac{5\\lambda}d$.<br>$\\frac\\pi6=\\frac{5\\lambda}d\\Rightarrow d=\\frac{30\\lambda}\\pi=\\frac{30\\times0.628\\ \\mu\\text{m}}{3.14}\\approx6\\ \\mu\\text{m}$."
