          "solution": "With $t=x^{1/3}$: $\\frac{x+1}{x^{2/3}-x^{1/3}+1}=\\frac{t^3+1}{t^2-t+1}=t+1=x^{1/3}+1$.<br>With $s=x^{1/2}$: $\\frac{x-1}{x-x^{1/2}}=\\frac{s^2-1}{s(s-1)}=\\frac{s+1}{s}=1+x^{-1/2}$.<br>The bracket equals $x^{1/3}-x^{-1/2}$. General term: $\\binom{10}{r}\\left(x^{1/3}\\right)^{10-r}\\left(-x^{-1/2}\\right)^r$, power of $x$: $\\frac{10-r}3-\\frac r2=0\\Rightarrow r=4$.<br>Term $=\\binom{10}4=210$.<br><b>Answer: (1)</b>"
