          "solution": "The denominator $\\to0$, so the numerator must $\\to0$: $\\gamma-1=0\\Rightarrow\\gamma=1$.<br>Then the numerator $=x^2\\sin\\alpha x\\approx\\alpha x^3$. Denominator: $\\sin2x-\\beta x=(2-\\beta)x-\\frac43x^3+\\dots$<br>For a finite non-zero limit the $x$ term must vanish: $\\beta=2$. Then the limit $=\\frac{\\alpha x^3}{-\\frac43x^3}=-\\frac{3\\alpha}4=3\\Rightarrow\\alpha=-4$.<br>$\\beta+\\gamma-\\alpha=2+1+4=7$.<br><b>Answer: (1)</b>"
