          "solution": "The lines meet at $(3,0)$ and the point $(-9,4)$ lies in the angular region containing the negative $x$-axis, so every circle touching both lines has its centre on the bisector $y=0$: centre $(h,0)$.<br>Radius $=$ distance to $x+y=3$ $=\\frac{|h-3|}{\\sqrt2}$. Passing through $(-9,4)$: $(h+9)^2+16=\\frac{(h-3)^2}2$.<br>$2h^2+36h+194=h^2-6h+9\\Rightarrow h^2+42h+185=0\\Rightarrow h=-5$ or $h=-37$.<br>$r_1^2=\\frac{64}2=32,\\quad r_2^2=\\frac{1600}2=800$. Difference $=800-32=768$."
