          "solution": "$\\frac1{e^{x-1}}=e^{1-x}$, which decreases from $e\\approx2.718$ at $x=0$ to $0$ as $x\\to\\infty$.<br>$[e^{1-x}]=2$ for $0\\le x\\le1-\\ln2$ (since $e^{1-x}\\ge2$ there and $\\lt 3$); $=1$ for $1-\\ln2\\lt x\\le1$; $=0$ for $x\\gt 1$.<br>Integral $=2(1-\\ln2)+1\\cdot\\ln2=2-\\ln2$. Hence $\\alpha=2$ and $\\alpha^3=8$."
