          "solution": "Total selections: $\\binom{40}3=9880$.<br>Three terms in increasing G.P. with common ratio $\\frac pq$ ($p\\gt q$, $\\gcd(p,q)=1$) are $kq^2,\\ kpq,\\ kp^2$; we need $kp^2\\le40$.<br>Count of $k$: $(p,q)=(2,1):10$; $(3,1):4$; $(4,1):2$; $(5,1):1$; $(6,1):1$; $(3,2):4$; $(4,3):2$; $(5,2):1$; $(5,3):1$; $(5,4):1$; $(6,5):1$. Total favourable $=28$.<br>$P=\\frac{28}{9880}=\\frac7{2470}$, already in lowest terms ($2470=2\\cdot5\\cdot13\\cdot19$). $m+n=7+2470=2477$.<br><i>Note: the source paper's key (4954) comes from not reducing $\\frac{14}{4940}$; the fraction must be in lowest terms.</i>"
