          "solution": "$y\\ge|4-x^2|$ and $y\\le x^2$ need $x^2\\ge|4-x^2|$. For $x\\le2$ this gives $x\\ge\\sqrt2$. For $x\\gt 2$ it is always true, but together with $y\\le4$ the region needs $x^2-4\\le4$, i.e. $x\\le2\\sqrt2$.<br>For $\\sqrt2\\le x\\le2$: $4-x^2\\le y\\le x^2$. For $2\\le x\\le2\\sqrt2$: $x^2-4\\le y\\le4$.<br>Area $=\\int_{\\sqrt2}^{2}(2x^2-4)\\,dx+\\int_2^{2\\sqrt2}(8-x^2)\\,dx=\\left(\\frac{8\\sqrt2-8}3\\right)+\\left(\\frac{32\\sqrt2-40}3\\right)=\\frac{40\\sqrt2}3-16=\\frac{80\\sqrt2}6-16$.<br>$\\alpha=6,\\ \\beta=16\\Rightarrow\\alpha+\\beta=22$."
